From 9ef4e1d89aec2e3259f61590ebb1d408ea74cc5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:40:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Cache with proof: import-time reads of a test module
 serve its own tests; name lookups, sendto and C-level sockets are never
 cached; only detpy's own variables leave the environment input;
 home-assistant and pylint specs

* import-time reads are attributed to the innermost repository module body (i|<path>); a test module no other
  module imports gives them to its own tests only (click: a module-level importlib.metadata.version() in one
  test file made the project's METADATA an input of all 2,500 tests)
* socket.getaddrinfo/gethostbyname/gethostbyaddr of a non-numeric host, socket.sendto/sendmsg: never cached
* sockets opened by C extensions (no audit event): /proc/self/fd scanned at every context switch, a new
  internet socket makes the context uncacheable
* env baseline drops only DETPY_REEXEC, DETPY_PRECOMPILE_S, DETPY_PYC_CACHE, DETPY_BLOCKED_PLUGINS (the
  DETPY_ prefix rule hid user variables: test_environment_variable_read... failed)
* tests: loopback HTTP proxy (review R-002b) and loopback service not started by the test, name lookup,
  C-level socket held by a module fixture, import-time read scope

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YAF6Dgp7MTxUYBRZseFL3V
